## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/swirl.html
- Summary (EN): Swirl twists an image layer into one or more spiral-shaped deformation regions. Combined with noise layers it can add organic variation such as tides, tree knots or lichen on rocks.
- Résumé (FR) : Swirl tord une couche image en une ou plusieurs zones de déformation en spirale, dont les centres et les échelles peuvent venir de points de géométrie.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: sets output image size and metadata", "source: layer to twist", "points: geometry setting the swirl centres and scale values", "stength (spelled this way on the page): strength scale", "bulge: bulge scale", "radius: radius scale", "blendregion: blend region scale", "innerradius: inner radius scale", "innerblendregion: inner blend region scale", "rotate: rotate scale", "roundness: roundness scale", "The last eight inputs are optional, each sampled at every swirl centre"]

- Key parameters: ["Wrap Mode: Auto, Off (clamps at the boundary), On (wraps at the boundary)", "Filter: sampling filter when the deformation reads between pixels", "Tile Size: size of the base deformation region", "Parameter Mode: Uniform (same controls for all swirls) or Random (variation from a standard deviation)", "Translation: moves the deformation regions in image space", "Strength: spiral amount, positive counterclockwise, negative clockwise", "Bulge: radial deformation, lens-distortion effect", "Radius and Blend Region: size of the deformed area and its soft edge", "Inner Radius and Inner Blend Region: undeformed centre and its soft edge", "Rotate: rotation of the deformation ellipse, in degrees", "Roundness: 1 is circular, lower values are elliptical", "Number of Points: number of swirl centres, each with its own Position and scale controls", "Randomize (Seed, Position Random, Central Value, Scatter): random variation of the shape"]

- Caveats: ["When geometry is wired into points, the Match Attributes Names parameters replace the manual Swirl parameters", "Each Match Attributes field takes a point attribute name, and scales default to 1 if the attribute is not set", "The page lists the input as 'stength', which looks like a typo for strength, check the real input name in the network before wiring"]

